Classical paintings are artworks influenced by traditional artistic principles, historical movements, and established painting techniques. They often feature balanced compositions, carefully arranged subjects, harmonious proportions, and recognizable themes drawn from mythology, history, religion, or everyday life. These paintings generally emphasize technical precision, structured compositions, and traditional aesthetic values.
